<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Entitlements for a Developer ID signed, notarized build.

	Two exceptions, both demanded by Qt Quick rather than by dae:

	* QML compiles JavaScript to machine code at run time (QV4's JIT). The
	  hardened runtime refuses to relax W^X on its own, so a QML engine without
	  `allow-jit` aborts with an mmap failure on the first binding it evaluates.
	* Qt loads its platform, image-format and multimedia plugins by path from
	  the bundle. `macdeployqt` copies those dylibs verbatim and re-signs them,
	  but any plugin it missed in a future Qt release would be rejected by
	  library validation at load time — taking the window or the preview down
	  with it, with a log line nobody sees.

	Nothing else is granted: no network, file-system or AppleEvents exceptions,
	because a notarized app runs outside the sandbox and already has them.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
